WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:10.574
Wolfgang Amadeus Mozart was like any other young boy growing up in a small town.

2
00:00:10.575 --> 00:00:16.961
He would play hide-and-seek with his friends, chase the dog around the house, and sometimes get into trouble.

3
00:00:16.962 --> 00:00:21.302
But there was something very special about this boy.

4
00:00:21.303 --> 00:00:25.675
Mozart could play the harpsichord, the violin, and the organ perfectly,

5
00:00:25.676 --> 00:00:31.552
and his biggest fans were the Emperor of Austria, the King of France, and the Queen of England.

6
00:00:31.553 --> 00:00:35.924
And he wasn't even ten years old yet!

7
00:00:35.925 --> 00:00:40.622
Mozart was born in Salzburg, Austria, in 1756.

8
00:00:40.623 --> 00:00:46.606
His father Leopold Mozart was a violinist who played in the court of the Archbishop of Salzburg.

9
00:00:46.607 --> 00:00:54.897
His older sister Nannerl was also talented; she played the piano and sang very well.

10
00:00:54.898 --> 00:01:00.587
When Mozart was only four years old, his sister asked him if he'd like to play her harpsichord.

11
00:01:00.588 --> 00:01:06.626
Without a word, little Wolfgang sat down and repeated everything she had just played perfectly.

12
00:01:06.627 --> 00:01:13.699
His father was impressed and arranged for Wolfgang to play with him at the court of the archbishop.

13
00:01:13.700 --> 00:01:19.231
News of Mozart's talent soon reached the Emperor of Austria, who invited him to play in Vienna.

14
00:01:19.232 --> 00:01:24.810
The emperor asked Mozart to play without looking at his hands and covered the keyboard with a piece of cloth.

15
00:01:24.811 --> 00:01:28.109
Mozart played brilliantly and without any difficulty.

16
00:01:28.110 --> 00:01:35.818
The emperor was so impressed he gave the little boy a gold watch.

17
00:01:35.819 --> 00:01:40.264
With the help of his ambitious father, the young musician became a sensation.

18
00:01:40.265 --> 00:01:48.094
Mozart's father, Leopold, decided not to waste Wolfgang's talent and took him on numerous tours across Europe with his sister.

19
00:01:48.095 --> 00:01:59.944
They showed their musical abilities to royal courts, which were the centers of power and money.

20
00:01:59.945 --> 00:02:02.079
Life on the road wasn't easy.

21
00:02:02.080 --> 00:02:07.215
Back then, not many people traveled across Europe, let alone a young child like Wolfgang.

22
00:02:07.216 --> 00:02:13.945
The Mozarts traveled by stagecoach, the trips were hard; and many of the roads were unpaved and dangerous.

23
00:02:13.946 --> 00:02:19.734
Wolfgang and his sister often got sick on the road.

24
00:02:19.735 --> 00:02:23.091
Everyone wanted to hear the little genius from Salzburg.

25
00:02:23.092 --> 00:02:25.269
Mozart was very busy.

26
00:02:25.270 --> 00:02:31.501
By the time Wolfgang was seven years old, he had played in front of many powerful kings and queens of Europe.

27
00:02:31.502 --> 00:02:39.414
He was very popular.

28
00:02:39.415 --> 00:02:45.702
Once Mozart was invited to spend Christmas with the king and queen of France and play in their castle.

29
00:02:45.703 --> 00:02:48.379
Everyone was deeply moved by his music.

30
00:02:48.380 --> 00:02:57.226
Right after playing, Wolfgang jumped up and hugged the queen, completely unaware of the rules of the royal court.

31
00:02:57.227 --> 00:03:02.687
After playing in France, Wolfgang headed to London to give a concert at the English court.

32
00:03:02.688 --> 00:03:08.109
Queen Charlotte, who had a beautiful singing voice, asked him to accompany her on the harpsichord.

33
00:03:08.110 --> 00:03:10.421
Mozart made a big impression.

34
00:03:10.422 --> 00:03:18.649
The queen was so touched by the little boy she even gave him a kiss! Everyone adored Mozart.

35
00:03:18.650 --> 00:03:24.615
Even though Mozart played for royalty and wealthy aristocrats, he was still very much a kid.

36
00:03:24.616 --> 00:03:28.136
He could go straight from playing music to playing marbles.

37
00:03:28.137 --> 00:03:38.247
Once, he stopped playing his harpsichord to chase a cat and didn't go back to finish the concert.

38
00:03:38.248 --> 00:03:44.385
When Mozart visited the Sistine Chapel in Rome, he was deeply touched by the church music he heard there.

39
00:03:44.386 --> 00:03:48.512
The beauty of the place and the sweet sounds coming from the organ overwhelmed him.

40
00:03:48.513 --> 00:03:50.890
It was as if angels were singing.

41
00:03:50.891 --> 00:03:54.963
Mozart decided that he wanted to write beautiful music one day too.

42
00:03:54.964 --> 00:03:59.869
Playing someone else's music was not enough for him.

43
00:03:59.870 --> 00:04:04.304
Unfortunately many of the aristocrats were losing interest in Mozart.

44
00:04:04.305 --> 00:04:09.601
After one unsuccessful concert in France, Mozart decided to go back to Salzburg.

45
00:04:09.602 --> 00:04:18.229
He stopped touring to concentrate on composing music.

46
00:04:18.230 --> 00:04:21.565
Once back home, Mozart began to write music.

47
00:04:21.566 --> 00:04:25.910
His early years on the road were very important for his development as a composer.

48
00:04:25.911 --> 00:04:30.448
In his music, he portrayed what he had seen and heard on his travels.

49
00:04:30.449 --> 00:04:37.659
For the rest of his life, Mozart would compose some of the most beautiful music ever written.

50
00:04:37.660 --> 00:04:42.634
Mozart's talent for composition was a different type of genius from his talent as a musician.

51
00:04:42.635 --> 00:04:49.595
Mozart knew how to capture emotion in beautiful melodies, and the style of his compositions remained playful and free.

52
00:04:49.596 --> 00:05:01.294
Also, Mozart never dedicated himself to just one type of music, but wrote operas, symphonies, and church music.

53
00:05:01.295 --> 00:05:05.693
Music was Mozart's language, and he used it to tell many different stories.

54
00:05:05.694 --> 00:05:09.452
He was a true genius and a passionate artist ahead of his time.

55
00:05:09.453 --> 00:05:20.324
His compositions continue to touch the hearts of listeners today, bringing them to a beautiful world through his music.

